  "title": "Hyundai Motor India's Connected-vehicle Expansion and Mid-size SUV Leadership",
  "summary": "Hyundai Motor India aims to expand its connected-vehicle technology and achieve 10 lakh units of connected cars by 2027, with a 250,000 unit annual target for its mid-size SUV segment in 2027. The company plans to maintain leadership in the fast-growing mid-SUV segment, leveraging its AI-powered technology platform.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Hyundai Motor India expects connected-vehicle penetration to rise as customers seek greater safety and convenience, with sales targeted to cross 2 million by 2030.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Hyundai aims to achieve 10 lakh connected cars by 2027, leveraging its proprietary AI-powered technology platform.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Hyundai Motor India plans to sell at least 2.50 lakh units of its Creta and new Bayon in 2027, with the segment leadership in the mid-SUV segment.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
