      "title": "Hyundai targets 250,000 mid-size SUV sales in 2027 on Creta, Bayon push",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/auto/hyundai-mid-size-suv-sales-2027-creta-bayon-tarun-garg-126102600623_1.html",
      "description": "MD and CEO Tarun Garg said the target is a baseline rather than a ceiling, as Hyundai expects the Creta and Bayon to appeal to different sets of mid-size SUV buyers",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-26T09:03:45"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hyundai targets annual sales of 250,000 units from new Bayon, Creta",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/auto/hyundai-targets-annual-sales-of-250-000-units-from-new-bayon-creta-126102600463_1.html",
      "description": "Hyundai Motor India aims to sell at least 2.50 lakh units of its Creta and new Bayon in 2027, as it looks to maintain leadership in the fast-growing mid-size SUV segment, according to its Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer Tarun Garg.\n\"Along with Creta and Bayon, we are looking at a volume of over 250,000 units per annum going forward. With this volume, very clearly, we can continue with our segment leadership in the mid-SUV segment. And 250,000 units is not a limit; it is a baseline; we will continue to grow,\" Garg told reporters while launching the new Bayon SUV.\nThe mid-size utility vehicle segment, models between 4-4.4 meters in length, including SUVs and MPVs, sold around 9 lakh units in the last financial year, as per the data from the Society of India Automobile Manufacturers.\nHyundai sold close to 2 lakh units annually in this segment in the last two financial years with Creta alone, and the segment accounted for close to 35 per cent of Hyundai's total domestic ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-26T08:14:06"
    }
  ]
